\begin{document}

\begin{abstract}
  We introduce the continuous version
  of the (unstable) smashing spectrum functor.
  In the stable case,
  it assigns to each dualizably symmetric monoidal
  stable presentable \(\infty\)-category
  a stably compact space
  whose open subsets
  correspond to very Schwartz idempotents—a certain class
  of idempotents we define.
  As an application,
  we prove Tannaka duality for
  spectral sheaves on stably compact spaces,
  including the case of compact Hausdorff spaces.
\end{abstract}



