The subtraction of the equations for \(S\) and \(\hat{S}\), \(E\) and \(\hat{E}\), \(I_1\) and \(\hat{I}_1\), \(I_2\) and \(\hat{I}_2\), \(T\) and \(\hat{T}\), \(A\) and \(\hat{A}\) are performed. Next, each equation is multiplied by a function that corresponds to it, and the resulting product is integrated across the time range ranging from \(t_0\) to \(t_f\). In light of this,
\begin{align*}
