Similarly, we derive the inequalities for $m_2$ and $\hat{m}_2$, $m_3$ and $\hat{m}_3$, $m_4$ and $\hat{m}_4$, $m_5$ and $\hat{m}_5$, $m_6$ and $\hat{m}_6$, $n_2$ and $\hat{n}_2$, $n_3$ and $\hat{n}_3$, $n_4$ and $\hat{n}_4$, $n_5$ and $\hat{n}_5$, $n_6$ and $\hat{n}_6$. Summing all the inequalities, we have,
\begin{align*}
	&\frac{1}{2} \big[(m_1 - \hat{m}_1)^2(t_f) + (m_2 - \hat{m}_2)^2(t_f) + (m_3 - \hat{m}_3)^2(t_f) + (m_4 - \hat{m}_4)^2(t_f) + (m_5 - \hat{m}_5)^2(t_f) \\
