%(a) these pulse trains have closer similarities to a dnoidal wave than noted previously; (b) previous analyses are extended to the case of Doppler broadening; (c) the similarity extends to systems with homogeneous broadening; (d) interesting changeover from SIT to propagation in steady state; 
%(e) for V-systems, existence of dnoidal-wave-induced transparency analogous to soliton-induced transparency, with analytical description of the former, and change over from SIT to EIT; 
%(f) the two fields propagate in step even though the propagation coefficients differ and Eq.~(\ref{eq:Delta}) is not fulfilled; (g) weak field V-EIT; 
%(h) for V-systems with a weak probe field, the latter propagates over much longer distances than without the assistance of the coupling field; 
%(i) stable two-colour dnoidal-like waves with two strong fields even with unequal propagation constants; 
%(j) V-system with a strong probe field: here the co-propagation is not underpinned by the analytical model as no analytical solution is known for that case, greater penetration for both fields, strong field V-EIT;
