\begin{proof}
Since a product of any elementary matrix is regular over $R$, the matrix $U$ in step 3 is regular over $R$. Then $A$ is also left regular over $R$ since it holds that
\[ B = (E_n | O_{n\times(m-n)})U^{-1} \in R^{n \times m}\]
and $BA = E_n$, which forces $\langle F \rangle = \langle G \rangle$.
