    Note that $\theta$, called the Markov contraction coefficient, is a constant determined by the graph structure and the transition probabilities of the Markov chain $\{\Psi^{(t)}\}$. It satisfies $0 \leq \theta < 1$ and remains independent of the number of samples $T$ drawn from the process.
