Observe that any minimal system is cohomologically $1$-connected, that is, it satisfies $\underline{H}^0(\sM)=\mathbb{Q}$ and $\underline{H}^1(\sM)=0$. It can be shown that being cohomologically $1$-connected is sufficient for a diagram of $\DGA$s to have a {\it minimal model.} 


