        {\bfseries ALenia glider persistence with respect to $\Delta t$ and $k_r$ shows non-Platonic loss of autopoiesis}. Persistence in accumulated time units is indicated by dark colors, with a transition from blue to green at the arbitrary threshold of 10 time units, the maximum simulation time.  
        %Darker shades indicate longer persistence, with accumulated time units $\geq 10$ shown in green and $< 10$ in blue. 
        `X', triangle, and star symbols mark $\Delta t = 0.26$, $0.20$, and $0.17$ from Figure 1, respectively. The lower persistence map is a zoom to the region in the small orange rectangle indicated by the arrow, showing retained details of apparent fractal structure.  
    }
